libimud (1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imud_data_t gains the wire-v17 MEKF diagnostic fields (append-only,
    ABI preserved): innov_weight and innov_reject report how hard the
    filter is having to distrust its sensors, nis_accel and nis_mag
    report whether the noise model itself is right (1.0 = the filter's
    covariance is consistent with the innovations it sees, higher means
    over-confident). Existing binaries keep working unchanged and do not
    need recompiling; the SONAME stays libimud.so.0.
  * Documented: the Euler attitude fields (pitch, roll, yaw, heading_deg,
    rate_of_turn) are ZYX intrinsic angles and are singular at pitch
    +/-90 deg by construction. Consumers that can encounter steep pitch
    must read quat_*, which is never singular. No code change — the
    quaternion has always been there.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

libimud (1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New imud_connect_tcp(host, port): connect to a daemon's [stream] TCP
    listener ([stream] tcp_enabled, default port 10112) for the same
    lossless framed packets as imud_connect_stream, over the network.
    Additive — new symbol version node IMUD_1; the SONAME stays
    libimud.so.0 and existing binaries are unaffected.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

libimud (1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imud_data_t.temp_c now carries the real IMU die temperature — the daemon
    never enabled FIFO temperature batching before 1.5, so the field was a
    25.0 degC placeholder in every prior release. No API/ABI change.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700

libimud (1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imud_data_t gains the wire-v14 fields (append-only, ABI preserved):
    wave_height_m, wave_period_s, roll_period_s, roll_amplitude,
    pitch_period_s, pitch_amplitude, mag_anomaly, mag_residual; new
    IMUD_FLAG_WAVE_VALID / IMUD_FLAG_ENGINE_ON. Existing binaries keep
    working without recompilation.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:35:35 -0700

libimud (1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: ABI-stable client shared library (libimud.so.0) for
    imud's binary telemetry — AF_UNIX stream and UDP transports, packet
    validation, and an append-only imud_data_t view so applications survive
    imud upgrades without recompiling. Ships imud.h and pkg-config metadata;
    the imud bridges are its first consumers.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700
